// apt download resilience for the kiosk's unattended upgrades.
// Installs to /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/80acquire-retries (system file; needs root).
//
// Why: the ~06:00 unattended-upgrade run fires seconds after the daily cold boot,
// while Wi-Fi is still settling (this site's Wi-Fi is flaky - see README
// "wifi-watchdog" and the 06:00 boot-join note). A transient fetch failure or a
// stalled mirror connection would otherwise fail the whole run, leaving the
// upgrade for a manual pass. These apt-wide settings make it retry and time out
// instead of hanging or aborting.
//
// Retries covers the download/fetch phase - the usual failure mode on flaky
// Wi-Fi. It does NOT retry a failed dpkg configure; unattended-upgrades already
// runs in minimal dpkg steps (Minimal-Steps, default on) so an interrupted run
// resumes cleanly on the next day's trigger.

// Re-attempt a failed package fetch up to 3 times before giving up.
Acquire::Retries "3";

// Bound a stalled connection so one dead mirror can't hang the run to the 01:00
// halt. Seconds; applies to the whole request (connect + transfer).
Acquire::http::Timeout "60";
Acquire::https::Timeout "60";
